# Permissions

This file owns the access vocabulary and enforcement model.

## Vocabulary

- `view` browse data.
- `create` add records.
- `edit` or `update` change records.
- `delete` remove records.
- `manage` configure module scope.
- `export` export data or reports.
- `assign` assign records or staff.
- `approve` approve workflow steps.
- Module-specific verbs may be added when needed, such as `dispense`, `request`, `report`, or `prescribe`.

## Access Model

Permissions may attach to users, roles, modules, and subscription packages.

Effective access = `union(role/module/user grants) ∩ subscription ∩ ABAC`.

Users may hold multiple roles and module assignments, but access must never exceed the active subscription or ABAC scope.

## ABAC

- Scope checks must consider tenant, facility, department, unit, ward, room, bed, record ownership, assignment, and status.
- `own` and `assigned` should be preferred over broad `view all` or `manage all`.
- Every permission decision must be recordable and auditable.

